/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State Dirichlet's Conditions for the expansion of a periodic function f\(x\) in a Fourier series. State the convergence theorem for continuous points and jump discontinuities.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Dirichlet's Conditions:) Tj
T*
(   Let f\(x\) be a periodic function defined on an interval of length 2L \(or 2pi\):) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Condition 1: f\(x\) is single-valued and bounded everywhere on [-L, L], meaning there exists) Tj
T*
(   a finite constant M > 0 such that |f\(x\)| <= M for all x.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Condition 2: f\(x\) is piecewise continuous, possessing at most a finite number of finite) Tj
T*
(   jump discontinuities in any single period.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Condition 3: f\(x\) is piecewise monotonic, possessing at most a finite number of local) Tj
T*
(   maxima and local minima in any single period.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dirichlet's Convergence Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   If f\(x\) satisfies Dirichlet's conditions on [-L, L], then the Fourier series:) Tj
T*
(   S\(x\) = a0 / 2 + sum_{n=1}^infinity [ an * cos\(n*pi*x / L\) + bn * sin\(n*pi*x / L\) ]) Tj
T*
(   converges for all real x, and its sum S\(x\) satisfies:) Tj
T*
(   - At every point of continuity x:) Tj
T*
(   S\(x\) = f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - At every point of jump discontinuity x0:) Tj
T*
(   S\(x0\) = \(1/2\) * [ f\(x0+\) + f\(x0-\) ],) Tj
T*
(   where f\(x0+\) = lim_{h -> 0+} f\(x0 + h\) is the right-hand limit, and f\(x0-\) = lim_{h -> 0+} f\(x0) Tj
T*
(   - h\) is the left-hand limit.) Tj
T*
(   - At the endpoints x = -L and x = L:) Tj
T*
(   S\(-L\) = S\(L\) = \(1/2\) * [ f\(-L+\) + f\(L-\) ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Prove the Orthogonality Relations of the trigonometric system {1, cos\(nx\), sin\(nx\)} on the interval [-pi, pi] for all positive integers m and n.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Integral 1: int_{-pi}^pi cos\(mx\) * cos\(nx\) dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Use product-to-sum identity: cos A * cos B = \(1/2\) * [ cos\(A + B\) + cos\(A - B\) ].) Tj
T*
(   cos\(mx\) * cos\(nx\) = \(1/2\) * [ cos\(\(m + n\)x\) + cos\(\(m - n\)x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(a\): m != n:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi cos\(mx\)*cos\(nx\) dx = \(1/2\) * [ sin\(\(m+n\)x\) / \(m+n\) + sin\(\(m-n\)x\) / \(m-n\)) Tj
T*
(   ]_{-pi}^pi.) Tj
T*
(   Since sin\(k*pi\) = sin\(-k*pi\) = 0 for all integers k:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi cos\(mx\) * cos\(nx\) dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(b\): m = n != 0:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi cos^2\(nx\) dx = int_{-pi}^pi [ \(1 + cos 2nx\) / 2 ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * [ x + sin\(2nx\) / \(2n\) ]_{-pi}^pi = \(1/2\) * [ pi - \(-pi\) + 0 ] = pi.) Tj
T*
(   2. Integral 2: int_{-pi}^pi sin\(mx\) * sin\(nx\) dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Use identity: sin A * sin B = \(1/2\) * [ cos\(A - B\) - cos\(A + B\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(a\): m != n:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi sin\(mx\)*sin\(nx\) dx = \(1/2\) * [ sin\(\(m-n\)x\)/\(m-n\) - sin\(\(m+n\)x\)/\(m+n\) ]_{-pi}^pi =) Tj
T*
(   0.) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(b\): m = n != 0:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi sin^2\(nx\) dx = int_{-pi}^pi [ \(1 - cos 2nx\) / 2 ] dx = \(1/2\) * [ 2*pi - 0 ] = pi.) Tj
T*
(   3. Integral 3: int_{-pi}^pi sin\(mx\) * cos\(nx\) dx:) Tj
T*
(   - The function sin\(mx\) is odd, and cos\(nx\) is even.) Tj
T*
(   - The product sin\(mx\) * cos\(nx\) is an ODD function for all m, n.) Tj
T*
(   - The definite integral of an odd function over symmetric interval [-pi, pi] is identically) Tj
T*
ET

