(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Euler's Formulas for the Fourier coefficients a0, an, and bn of a periodic function f\(x\) on the interval [-pi, pi] using orthogonality relations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fourier Series Representation:) Tj
T*
(   Assume f\(x\) can be expanded as:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = a0 / 2 + sum_{k=1}^infinity [ ak * cos\(kx\) + bk * sin\(kx\) ]. \(Eq. 1\)) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of a0:) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate both sides of Eq. 1 with respect to x from -pi to pi:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) dx = \(a0 / 2\) * int_{-pi}^pi 1 dx + sum_{k=1}^infinity [ ak * int_{-pi}^pi) Tj
T*
(   cos\(kx\) dx + bk * int_{-pi}^pi sin\(kx\) dx ].) Tj
T*
(   - For all k >= 1: int_{-pi}^pi cos\(kx\) dx = 0, and int_{-pi}^pi sin\(kx\) dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - int_{-pi}^pi 1 dx = 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) dx = \(a0 / 2\) * \(2*pi\) = a0 * pi) Tj
T*
(   => a0 = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of an \(for fixed n >= 1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply both sides of Eq. 1 by cos\(nx\) and integrate from -pi to pi:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\)*cos\(nx\) dx = \(a0/2\)*int_{-pi}^pi cos\(nx\) dx + sum_{k=1}^infinity) Tj
T*
(   ak*int_{-pi}^pi cos\(kx\)*cos\(nx\) dx + sum_{k=1}^infinity bk*int_{-pi}^pi sin\(kx\)*cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - By orthogonality:) Tj
T*
(   * int_{-pi}^pi cos\(nx\) dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   * int_{-pi}^pi sin\(kx\)*cos\(nx\) dx = 0 for all k.) Tj
T*
(   * int_{-pi}^pi cos\(kx\)*cos\(nx\) dx = 0 for all k != n, and equals pi when k = n.) Tj
T*
(   - The entire infinite sum collapses to a single term:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\)*cos\(nx\) dx = an * pi) Tj
T*
(   => an = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * cos\(nx\) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Derivation of bn \(for fixed n >= 1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply both sides of Eq. 1 by sin\(nx\) and integrate from -pi to pi:) Tj
T*
(   By identical orthogonality relations, all terms vanish except bk for k = n:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\)*sin\(nx\) dx = bn * pi) Tj
T*
(   => bn = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * sin\(nx\) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
