BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the Fourier series of the square wave: f\(x\) = -1 for -pi < x < 0, and f\(x\) = +1 for 0 < x < pi. Hence, deduce Leibniz's Gregory series for pi/4.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Check Symmetry of f\(x\):) Tj
T*
(   - For x in \(0, pi\): f\(-x\) = -1 = -f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, f\(x\) is an ODD function on \(-pi, pi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Consequently:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = 0 and an = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   The Fourier series consists exclusively of sine terms \(bn\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute Fourier Coefficient bn:) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi f\(x\) * sin\(nx\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi 1 * sin\(nx\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / pi\) * [ -cos\(nx\) / n ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
