(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Prove that if f\(x\) is an even function on [-pi, pi], its Fourier series reduces to a Fourier Cosine Series with bn = 0, and if f\(x\) is an odd function, it reduces to a Fourier Sine Series with a0 = an = 0.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Properties of Integrals of Even and Odd Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - If g\(x\) is an even function on [-a, a]: int_{-a}^a g\(x\) dx = 2 * int_0^a g\(x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - If g\(x\) is an odd function on [-a, a]: int_{-a}^a g\(x\) dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Case 1: f\(x\) is an Even Function \(f\(-x\) = f\(x\)\):) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient a0:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Since f\(x\) is even: a0 = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi f\(x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient an:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Since f\(x\) is even and cos\(nx\) is even, the product f\(x\)*cos\(nx\) is even:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi f\(x\) * cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient bn:) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * sin\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Since f\(x\) is even and sin\(nx\) is odd, the product f\(x\)*sin\(nx\) is an ODD function:) Tj
T*
(   bn = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus: f\(x\) = a0/2 + sum_{n=1}^infinity an * cos\(nx\) \(Fourier Cosine Series\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Case 2: f\(x\) is an Odd Function \(f\(-x\) = -f\(x\)\):) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient a0:) Tj
T*
(   Since f\(x\) is odd: a0 = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient an:) Tj
T*
(   Product f\(x\)*cos\(nx\) is \(odd\)*\(even\) = ODD:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * cos\(nx\) dx = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Coefficient bn:) Tj
T*
(   Product f\(x\)*sin\(nx\) is \(odd\)*\(odd\) = EVEN:) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi f\(x\) * sin\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus: f\(x\) = sum_{n=1}^infinity bn * sin\(nx\) \(Fourier Sine Series\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
