(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the Fourier series of f\(x\) = x^2 on [-pi, pi]. Hence, deduce: \(i\) sum_{n=1}^infinity 1/n^2 = pi^2/6 \(Euler's Basel Problem\), \(ii\) sum_{n=1}^infinity \(-1\)^\(n+1\)/n^2 = pi^2/12, and \(iii\) sum_{n=1}^infinity 1/\(2n-1\)^2 = pi^2/8.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Symmetry and Coefficients:) Tj
T*
(   f\(-x\) = \(-x\)^2 = x^2 = f\(x\). f\(x\) is an EVEN function on [-pi, pi].) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: bn = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute a0:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x^2 dx = \(2 / pi\) * [ x^3 / 3 ]_0^pi = \(2 / pi\) * \(pi^3 / 3\) = 2*pi^2) Tj
T*
(   / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Constant term: a0 / 2 = pi^2 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compute an:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x^2 * cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Integrate by parts: u = x^2, dv = cos\(nx\) dx \(v = sin\(nx\)/n, v2 = -cos\(nx\)/n^2, v3 =) Tj
T*
(   -sin\(nx\)/n^3\):) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / pi\) * [ x^2 * \(sin nx / n\) - 2x * \(-cos nx / n^2\) + 2 * \(-sin nx / n^3\) ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / pi\) * [ 0 + 2*pi*cos\(n*pi\) / n^2 - 0 ] - 0) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / pi\) * [ 2*pi * \(-1\)^n / n^2 ] = 4 * \(-1\)^n / n^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Assemble the Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(   x^2 = pi^2 / 3 + sum_{n=1}^infinity [ 4 * \(-1\)^n / n^2 ] * cos\(nx\)) Tj
T*
ET

