/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the Fourier series of f\(x\) = |x| on [-pi, pi]. Hence, deduce that: 1/1^2 + 1/3^2 + 1/5^2 + ... = pi^2 / 8.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Check Symmetry of f\(x\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(-x\) = |-x| = |x| = f\(x\). Thus f\(x\) is an EVEN function on [-pi, pi].) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: bn = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute a0:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x dx = \(2 / pi\) * [ x^2 / 2 ]_0^pi = \(2 / pi\) * \(pi^2 / 2\) = pi.) Tj
T*
(   Constant term: a0 / 2 = pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compute an:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x * cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Integrate by parts: u = x, dv = cos\(nx\) dx => du = dx, v = sin\(nx\)/n.) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / pi\) * [ x * sin\(nx\) / n ]_0^pi - \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi [ sin\(nx\) / n ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = 0 - \(2 / \(n * pi\)\) * [ -cos\(nx\) / n ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / \(n^2 * pi\)\) * [ cos\(n*pi\) - cos\(0\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / \(n^2 * pi\)\) * [ \(-1\)^n - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate an for Even and Odd n:) Tj
T*
(   - If n is even: \(-1\)^n = 1 => 1 - 1 = 0 => an = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - If n is odd: \(-1\)^n = -1 => -1 - 1 = -2 => an = -4 / \(n^2 * pi\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Assemble the Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(   |x| = pi / 2 - \(4 / pi\) * sum_{k=1}^infinity [ cos\(\(2k - 1\)x\) / \(2k - 1\)^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = pi / 2 - \(4 / pi\) * [ \(cos x\)/1^2 + \(cos 3x\)/3^2 + \(cos 5x\)/5^2 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Deduction:) Tj
T*
(   Substitute x = 0 \(point of continuity where f\(0\) = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   0 = pi / 2 - \(4 / pi\) * [ 1/1^2 + 1/3^2 + 1/5^2 + ... ]) Tj
T*
(   \(4 / pi\) * [ 1/1^2 + 1/3^2 + 1/5^2 + ... ] = pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Multiply both sides by pi / 4:) Tj
T*
(   1/1^2 + 1/3^2 + 1/5^2 + ... = \(pi / 2\) * \(pi / 4\) = pi^2 / 8.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The Fourier series is pi/2 - \(4/pi\)*sum cos\(\(2n-1\)x\)/\(2n-1\)^2, and sum 1/\(2n-1\)^2 = pi^2/8 is) Tj
T*
(   established.) Tj
T*
