(>> Solution to Question 10:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Fourier series expansion formulas for a function f\(x\) defined on an arbitrary symmetric interval [-L, L] by change of scale of variable.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation via Variable Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   - Let f\(x\) be defined on [-L, L] with period 2L.) Tj
T*
(   - We map the interval [-L, L] to [-pi, pi] by introducing the dimensionless variable t:) Tj
T*
(   t = pi * x / L => x = L * t / pi.) Tj
T*
(   - When x = -L, t = -pi; when x = L, t = pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Define F\(t\) = f\(L * t / pi\) on [-pi, pi].) Tj
T*
(   2. Standard Fourier Series of F\(t\) on [-pi, pi]:) Tj
T*
(   F\(t\) = a0 / 2 + sum_{n=1}^infinity [ an * cos\(nt\) + bn * sin\(nt\) ],) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi F\(t\) dt) Tj
T*
(   an = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi F\(t\) * cos\(nt\) dt) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(1 / pi\) * int_{-pi}^pi F\(t\) * sin\(nt\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   3. Transform Back to Variable x:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
