(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the Fourier series of f\(x\) = x on the interval [-2, 2] \(period 2L = 4, so L = 2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Symmetry and Coefficients:) Tj
T*
(   f\(-x\) = -x = -f\(x\). f\(x\) is an ODD function on [-2, 2].) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = 0 and an = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute Fourier Coefficient bn \(with L = 2\):) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / L\) * int_0^L f\(x\) * sin\(n*pi*x / L\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 2\) * int_0^2 x * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^2 x * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Integrate by Parts:) Tj
T*
(   Let u = x, dv = sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) dx:) Tj
T*
(   du = dx, v = - [ 2 / \(n*pi\) ] * cos\(n*pi*x / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   bn = [ - 2x / \(n*pi\) * cos\(n*pi*x / 2\) ]_0^2 - int_0^2 [ - 2 / \(n*pi\) * cos\(n*pi*x / 2\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ - 4 / \(n*pi\) * cos\(n*pi\) - 0 ] + [ 2 / \(n*pi\) ] * [ 2 / \(n*pi\) * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) ]_0^2) Tj
T*
(   = - 4 * \(-1\)^n / \(n*pi\) + 0) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * \(-1\)^\(n + 1\) / \(n * pi\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Assemble the Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = sum_{n=1}^infinity [ 4 * \(-1\)^\(n+1\) / \(n*pi\) ] * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(4 / pi\) * [ sin\(pi*x / 2\) - \(1/2\)*sin\(2*pi*x / 2\) + \(1/3\)*sin\(3*pi*x / 2\) - ... ].) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The Fourier series on [-2, 2] is \(4/pi\) * sum \(-1\)^\(n+1\) * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) / n.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
