(>> Solution to Question 12:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the Fourier series of f\(x\) = 2x - x^2 on the interval [0, 3] with period T = 3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Identify Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   Interval [0, 2L] = [0, 3] => 2L = 3 => L = 3/2 = 1.5.) Tj
T*
(   Fundamental frequency factor: n*pi*x / L = 2*n*pi*x / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute a0:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(1 / L\) * int_0^\(2L\) f\(x\) dx = \(2 / 3\) * int_0^3 \(2x - x^2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ x^2 - x^3 / 3 ]_0^3) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ 9 - 27 / 3 ] = \(2 / 3\) * [ 9 - 9 ] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Thus: a0 / 2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compute an:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / 3\) * int_0^3 \(2x - x^2\) * cos\(2*n*pi*x / 3\) dx.) Tj
T*
ET

