(   Integrate by parts:) Tj
T*
(   u = 2x - x^2, u' = 2 - 2x, u'' = -2, u''' = 0.) Tj
T*
(   v = cos\(kx\), v1 = sin\(kx\)/k, v2 = -cos\(kx\)/k^2, v3 = -sin\(kx\)/k^3, where k = 2*n*pi / 3.) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / 3\) * [ \(2x - x^2\)*\(sin kx / k\) - \(2 - 2x\)*\(-cos kx / k^2\) + \(-2\)*\(-sin kx / k^3\)) Tj
T*
(   ]_0^3.) Tj
T*
(   Since sin\(k*3\) = sin\(2*n*pi\) = 0 and sin\(0\) = 0, the sine terms vanish at both limits:) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / 3\) * [ \(2 - 2x\)*cos\(kx\) / k^2 ]_0^3) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ \(2 - 6\)*cos\(2n*pi\) / k^2 - \(2 - 0\)*cos\(0\) / k^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ -4\(1\) / k^2 - 2\(1\) / k^2 ] = \(2 / 3\) * [ -6 / k^2 ] = -4 / k^2.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute k = 2*n*pi / 3 => k^2 = 4*n^2*pi^2 / 9:) Tj
T*
(   an = -4 / [ 4*n^2*pi^2 / 9 ] = - 9 / \(n^2 * pi^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Compute bn:) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / 3\) * int_0^3 \(2x - x^2\) * sin\(kx\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ \(2x - x^2\)*\(-cos kx / k\) - \(2 - 2x\)*\(-sin kx / k^2\) + \(-2\)*\(cos kx / k^3\) ]_0^3) Tj
T*
(   = \(2 / 3\) * [ - \(2x - x^2\)*cos\(kx\) / k - 2*cos\(kx\) / k^3 ]_0^3.) Tj
T*
(   At x = 3: -\(6 - 9\)\(1\)/k - 2\(1\)/k^3 = 3/k - 2/k^3.) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0: -\(0\)\(1\)/k - 2\(1\)/k^3 = -2/k^3.) Tj
T*
(   Difference = \(3/k - 2/k^3\) - \(-2/k^3\) = 3 / k.) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / 3\) * [ 3 / k ] = 2 / k = 2 / \(2*n*pi / 3\) = 3 / \(n * pi\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Assemble the Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = - \(9 / pi^2\) * sum_{n=1}^infinity [ cos\(2*n*pi*x / 3\) / n^2 ] + \(3 / pi\) *) Tj
T*
(   sum_{n=1}^infinity [ sin\(2*n*pi*x / 3\) / n ].) Tj
T*
