/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Half-Range Fourier Expansions. Detail how an even extension yields a Half-Range Cosine Series and an odd extension yields a Half-Range Sine Series on [0, L].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theory of Half-Range Expansions:) Tj
T*
(   - Suppose a function f\(x\) is defined only on a half-interval [0, L].) Tj
T*
(   - We have freedom to extend f\(x\) into the other half [-L, 0\) in two standard ways:) Tj
T*
(   2. Even Periodic Extension \(Half-Range Cosine Series\):) Tj
T*
(   - Define f_even\(x\) on [-L, L] by:) Tj
T*
(   f_even\(x\) = f\(x\) for x in [0, L], and f_even\(x\) = f\(-x\) for x in [-L, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since f_even\(x\) is an even function on [-L, L]:) Tj
T*
(   bn = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   - The Fourier series contains ONLY cosine terms:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = a0 / 2 + sum_{n=1}^infinity an * cos\(n*pi*x / L\),) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = \(2 / L\) * int_0^L f\(x\) dx) Tj
T*
(   an = \(2 / L\) * int_0^L f\(x\) * cos\(n*pi*x / L\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   3. Odd Periodic Extension \(Half-Range Sine Series\):) Tj
T*
(   - Define f_odd\(x\) on [-L, L] by:) Tj
T*
(   f_odd\(x\) = f\(x\) for x in \(0, L], and f_odd\(x\) = -f\(-x\) for x in [-L, 0\), with f_odd\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since f_odd\(x\) is an odd function on [-L, L]:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = 0 and an = 0 for all n >= 1.) Tj
T*
(   - The Fourier series contains ONLY sine terms:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = sum_{n=1}^infinity bn * sin\(n*pi*x / L\),) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / L\) * int_0^L f\(x\) * sin\(n*pi*x / L\) dx.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
