(   [Problem Statement]: Obtain the Half-Range Sine Series of f\(x\) = x*\(pi - x\) on the interval [0, pi]. Hence, deduce the sum: 1/1^3 - 1/3^3 + 1/5^3 - 1/7^3 + ... = pi^3 / 32.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the Half-Range Sine Coefficient bn \(L = pi\):) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi \(pi*x - x^2\) * sin\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Integrate by Parts:) Tj
T*
(   u = pi*x - x^2, u' = pi - 2x, u'' = -2, u''' = 0.) Tj
T*
(   v = sin\(nx\), v1 = -cos\(nx\)/n, v2 = -sin\(nx\)/n^2, v3 = cos\(nx\)/n^3.) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / pi\) * [ \(pi*x - x^2\)*\(-cos nx / n\) - \(pi - 2x\)*\(-sin nx / n^2\) + \(-2\)*\(cos nx / n^3\)) Tj
T*
(   ]_0^pi.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate at Limits:) Tj
T*
(   - First term vanishes at both limits since pi*x - x^2 = 0 at x = 0 and x = pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Second term vanishes since sin\(n*pi\) = sin\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Third term:) Tj
T*
(   At x = pi: -2 * cos\(n*pi\) / n^3 = -2 * \(-1\)^n / n^3.) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0: -2 * cos\(0\) / n^3 = -2 / n^3.) Tj
T*
(   Difference = [ -2*\(-1\)^n / n^3 ] - [ -2 / n^3 ] = \(2 / n^3\) * [ 1 - \(-1\)^n ].) Tj
T*
(   bn = \(2 / pi\) * \(2 / n^3\) * [ 1 - \(-1\)^n ] = \(4 / \(pi * n^3\)\) * [ 1 - \(-1\)^n ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Values for Even and Odd n:) Tj
T*
(   - If n is even: 1 - \(-1\)^n = 0 => bn = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - If n is odd \(n = 2k - 1\): 1 - \(-1\)^n = 2 => bn = 8 / \(pi * n^3\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Assemble the Half-Range Sine Series:) Tj
T*
(   x*\(pi - x\) = \(8 / pi\) * sum_{k=1}^infinity [ sin\(\(2k - 1\)x\) / \(2k - 1\)^3 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(8 / pi\) * [ \(sin x\)/1^3 + \(sin 3x\)/3^3 + \(sin 5x\)/5^3 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Deduction at x = pi / 2:) Tj
T*
(   - At x = pi / 2:) Tj
T*
(   f\(pi/2\) = \(pi/2\) * \(pi - pi/2\) = \(pi/2\) * \(pi/2\) = pi^2 / 4.) Tj
T*
(   sin\(pi/2\) = 1, sin\(3pi/2\) = -1, sin\(5pi/2\) = 1, sin\(7pi/2\) = -1.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute into series:) Tj
T*
(   pi^2 / 4 = \(8 / pi\) * [ 1/1^3 - 1/3^3 + 1/5^3 - 1/7^3 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply both sides by pi / 8:) Tj
T*
(   1/1^3 - 1/3^3 + 1/5^3 - 1/7^3 + ... = \(pi^2 / 4\) * \(pi / 8\) = pi^3 / 32.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The half-range sine series is established and the alternating cubic reciprocal sum evaluates to) Tj
T*
(   pi^3 / 32.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
