(   x*\(pi - x\) = pi^2 / 6 - sum_{m=1}^infinity [ cos\(2mx\) / m^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = pi^2 / 6 - [ \(cos 2x\)/1^2 + \(cos 4x\)/2^2 + \(cos 6x\)/3^2 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Deduction of Basel Problem \(sum 1/m^2\):) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0: f\(0\) = 0 => 0 = pi^2 / 6 - sum_{m=1}^infinity 1/m^2 => sum 1/m^2 = pi^2 / 6.) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Deduction of sum 1/m^4 using Parseval's Identity:) Tj
T*
(   - For half-range cosine series on [0, pi]:) Tj
T*
(   \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi [f\(x\)]^2 dx = a0^2 / 2 + sum_{m=1}^infinity am^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Left-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^pi [x*\(pi - x\)]^2 dx = int_0^pi \(pi^2*x^2 - 2pi*x^3 + x^4\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ pi^2*x^3/3 - 2pi*x^4/4 + x^5/5 ]_0^pi = pi^5 * [ 1/3 - 1/2 + 1/5 ] = pi^5 / 30.) Tj
T*
(   \(2 / pi\) * \(pi^5 / 30\) = pi^4 / 15.) Tj
T*
(   - a0^2 / 2 = \(pi^2 / 3\)^2 / 2 = pi^4 / 18.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   pi^4 / 15 = pi^4 / 18 + sum_{m=1}^infinity \(1 / m^2\)^2 = pi^4 / 18 + sum 1/m^4) Tj
T*
(   sum_{m=1}^infinity 1 / m^4 = pi^4 / 15 - pi^4 / 18 = \(6 - 5\)*pi^4 / 90 = pi^4 / 90.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The half-range cosine series is derived and sum 1/m^4 = pi^4 / 90 is proven.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
