(   [f\(x\)]^2 = x^2.) Tj
T*
(   int_{-pi}^pi x^2 dx = 2 * int_0^pi x^2 dx = 2 * [ x^3 / 3 ]_0^pi = 2 * pi^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   LHS = \(1 / pi\) * \(2*pi^3 / 3\) = 2*pi^2 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate Right-Hand Side:) Tj
T*
(   a0 = 0, an = 0.) Tj
T*
(   bn^2 = [ 2 * \(-1\)^\(n+1\) / n ]^2 = 4 / n^2.) Tj
T*
(   RHS = sum_{n=1}^infinity bn^2 = sum_{n=1}^infinity 4 / n^2 = 4 * sum_{n=1}^infinity 1 / n^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Equate LHS and RHS:) Tj
T*
(   2*pi^2 / 3 = 4 * sum_{n=1}^infinity 1 / n^2.) Tj
T*
(   Divide both sides by 4:) Tj
T*
(   sum_{n=1}^infinity 1 / n^2 = \(2*pi^2 / 3\) / 4 = pi^2 / 6.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Parseval's identity confirms Euler's Basel sum: sum_{n=1}^infinity 1/n^2 = pi^2 / 6.) Tj
