BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Complex \(Exponential\) Form of Fourier Series from the real trigonometric Fourier series using Euler's formula e^\(i*theta\) = cos\(theta\) + i*sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Real Trigonometric Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = a0 / 2 + sum_{n=1}^infinity [ an * cos\(nx\) + bn * sin\(nx\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Express Cosine and Sine via Complex Exponentials:) Tj
T*
(   cos\(nx\) = \(e^\(i*nx\) + e^\(-i*nx\)\) / 2) Tj
T*
(   sin\(nx\) = \(e^\(i*nx\) - e^\(-i*nx\)\) / \(2i\) = -i * \(e^\(i*nx\) - e^\(-i*nx\)\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Substitute into the Series:) Tj
T*
(   an * cos\(nx\) + bn * sin\(nx\) = an * [ \(e^\(i*nx\) + e^\(-i*nx\)\) / 2 ] - i * bn * [ \(e^\(i*nx\) -) Tj
T*
(   e^\(-i*nx\)\) / 2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(an - i*bn\) / 2 ] * e^\(i*nx\) + [ \(an + i*bn\) / 2 ] * e^\(-i*nx\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Define Complex Fourier Coefficients:) Tj
T*
(   - For n > 0: cn = \(an - i*bn\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - For n < 0: c_{-n} = \(an + i*bn\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - For n = 0: c0 = a0 / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Then:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) = c0 + sum_{n=1}^infinity cn * e^\(i*nx\) + sum_{n=1}^infinity c_{-n} * e^\(-i*nx\)) Tj
T*
(   = sum_{n=-infinity}^infinity cn * e^\(i*nx\).) Tj
T*
(   5. Integral Formula for cn:) Tj
T*
(   - cn = \(1/2\) * [ an - i*bn ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * [ \(1/pi\)*int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\)*cos\(nx\) dx - i*\(1/pi\)*int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\)*sin\(nx\) dx ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / \(2*pi\)\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * [ cos\(nx\) - i*sin\(nx\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / \(2*pi\)\) * int_{-pi}^pi f\(x\) * e^\(-i*nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - For an arbitrary interval [-L, L]:) Tj
T*
(   cn = \(1 / \(2*L\)\) * int_{-L}^L f\(x\) * e^\(-i*n*pi*x / L\) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
