(   [Problem Statement]: Perform practical harmonic analysis on the following 6-point periodic dataset to find the constant term and the first harmonic of the Fourier series: x = [0, 60, 120, 180, 240, 300] deg, y = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.7, 0.9, 1.1].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Setup Computational Table \(N = 6\):) Tj
T*
(   x \(deg\) y cos x sin x y*cos x y*sin x) Tj
T*
(   ----------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(   0 0.8 1.000 0.000 0.8000 0.0000) Tj
T*
(   60 0.6 0.500 0.866 0.3000 0.5196) Tj
T*
(   120 0.4 -0.500 0.866 -0.2000 0.3464) Tj
T*
(   180 0.7 -1.000 0.000 -0.7000 0.0000) Tj
T*
(   240 0.9 -0.500 -0.866 -0.4500 -0.7794) Tj
T*
(   300 1.1 0.500 -0.866 0.5500 -0.9526) Tj
T*
(   ----------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(   Sum: 4.5 0.3000 -0.8660) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Calculate Constant Term a0 / 2:) Tj
T*
(   Sum of y = 0.8 + 0.6 + 0.4 + 0.7 + 0.9 + 1.1 = 4.5.) Tj
T*
(   a0 / 2 = Mean of y = 4.5 / 6 = 0.75.) Tj
T*
(   a0 = 1.50.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Calculate First Harmonic Cosine Coefficient a1:) Tj
T*
