12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In biotechnology and endocrinology, circadian hormone secretion \(such as serum cortisol\) follows a 24-hour diurnal cycle. Model cortisol concentration C\(t\) = a0/2 + a1*cos\(pi*t/12\) + b1*sin\(pi*t/12\). Given measurements C\(0\)=15 ug/dL \(midnight\), C\(6\)=25 ug/dL \(6 AM\), C\(12\)=10 ug/dL \(noon\), C\(18\)=5 ug/dL \(6 PM\), compute the Fourier harmonics and determine the time of peak cortisol secretion.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the 4-Point Dataset over Period T = 24 hours \(N = 4\):) Tj
T*
(   - x = pi * t / 12 \(in radians\).) Tj
T*
(   - t = 0 h \(midnight\): x = 0 rad, C = 15 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   - t = 6 h \(6 AM\): x = pi/2 rad, C = 25 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   - t = 12 h \(noon\): x = pi rad, C = 10 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   - t = 18 h \(6 PM\): x = 3pi/2 rad, C = 5 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Calculate Mean Cortisol \(Baseline a0/2\):) Tj
T*
(   Sum of C = 15 + 25 + 10 + 5 = 55 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   a0 / 2 = Mean\(C\) = 55 / 4 = 13.75 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Calculate First Cosine Harmonic a1:) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 0: C * cos\(0\) = 15 * 1 = 15.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 6: C * cos\(pi/2\) = 25 * 0 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 12: C * cos\(pi\) = 10 * \(-1\) = -10.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 18: C * cos\(3pi/2\) = 5 * 0 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Sum = 15 + 0 - 10 + 0 = 5.) Tj
T*
(   a1 = \(2 / N\) * Sum = \(2 / 4\) * 5 = 2.5 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Calculate First Sine Harmonic b1:) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 0: C * sin\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 6: C * sin\(pi/2\) = 25 * 1 = 25.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 12: C * sin\(pi\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 18: C * sin\(3pi/2\) = 5 * \(-1\) = -5.) Tj
T*
(   Sum = 0 + 25 + 0 - 5 = 20.) Tj
T*
(   b1 = \(2 / N\) * Sum = \(2 / 4\) * 20 = 10.0 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Assemble Cortisol Fourier Model:) Tj
T*
(   C\(t\) = 13.75 + 2.5 * cos\(pi * t / 12\) + 10.0 * sin\(pi * t / 12\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Amplitude and Peak Time:) Tj
T*
(   - Amplitude A1 = sqrt\(a1^2 + b1^2\) = sqrt\(2.5^2 + 10.0^2\) = sqrt\(6.25 + 100\) = sqrt\(106.25\) ~) Tj
T*
(   10.31 ug/dL.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximize C\(t\): set dC/dt = 0:) Tj
T*
(   - 2.5 * \(pi/12\) * sin\(pi*t/12\) + 10.0 * \(pi/12\) * cos\(pi*t/12\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   => tan\(pi*t / 12\) = 10.0 / 2.5 = 4.0.) Tj
T*
(   pi*t / 12 = arctan\(4.0\) ~ 1.3258 radians \(75.96 degrees\).) Tj
T*
(   t_peak = 12 * 1.3258 / pi = 5.06 hours = 5 hours and 4 minutes AM.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
ET

