(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In Heart Rate Variability \(HRV\) analysis, explain how the Fourier power spectral density of the RR-interval tachogram is used to assess autonomic nervous system balance \(LF/HF ratio\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Heart Rate Variability \(HRV\) Tachogram:) Tj
T*
(   - The time elapsed between successive R-peaks of the QRS complex in an ECG is the RR-interval) Tj
T*
(   \(inter-beat interval IBI\).) Tj
T*
(   - A sequence of N sampled RR-intervals forms a discrete time series s\(k\) representing) Tj
T*
(   instantaneous heart rate fluctuations.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fourier Spectral Decomposition:) Tj
T*
(   - The RR-interval series is decomposed via discrete Fourier transform into its constituent) Tj
T*
(   frequency components:) Tj
T*
(   S\(f\) = sum_{k=0}^{N-1} s\(k\) * e^\(-i * 2*pi * f * k * Delta_t\).) Tj
T*
(   - The Power Spectral Density \(PSD\) is P\(f\) = |S\(f\)|^2 / N.) Tj
T*
(   3. Physiological Frequency Bands:) Tj
T*
(   - Very Low Frequency \(VLF, 0.0033 - 0.04 Hz\): Regulated by thermoregulation,) Tj
T*
(   renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system, and peripheral vasomotor tone.) Tj
T*
(   - Low Frequency \(LF, 0.04 - 0.15 Hz\): Reflects baroreceptor reflex activity, influenced by BOTH) Tj
T*
(   sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous systems.) Tj
T*
(   - High Frequency \(HF, 0.15 - 0.40 Hz\): Reflects respiratory sinus arrhythmia \(RSA\), modulated) Tj
T*
(   EXCLUSIVELY by the parasympathetic \(vagal\) nervous system.) Tj
T*
(   4. Autonomic Balance Index \(LF / HF Ratio\):) Tj
T*
(   - The total power in the LF and HF bands is computed by integrating the Fourier power spectrum:) Tj
T*
(   P_LF = int_{0.04}^{0.15} P\(f\) df, P_HF = int_{0.15}^{0.40} P\(f\) df.) Tj
T*
(   - Sympathovagal Balance:) Tj
T*
(   Ratio = P_LF / P_HF.) Tj
T*
(   - Clinical and Biotechnological Interpretation:) Tj
T*
(   * High LF/HF ratio \(> 2.0\): Indicates sympathetic dominance \(acute physical or mental stress,) Tj
T*
(   cardiac risk, hypertension, heart failure\).) Tj
T*
(   * Low LF/HF ratio \(< 1.0\): Indicates parasympathetic \(vagal\) dominance \(deep relaxation,) Tj
T*
(   aerobic fitness, recovery\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
